bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 0, "The largest cause of the 1x catalog mismatch (about 55 to 60 percent; mismatch components of 15 px or less are 53 to 68 percent on the six content pages) is the hinted LCD outline. Chrome 159 hints through Skia's Fontations backend (skrifa autohinter, kSlight, forced for glyf) and fills the path with SkScan_AAAPath. The engine's fill, LCD filter, preblend and composite are exact for its own outline (3 px of 1,760 against libskia); its outline is a knot approximation (_lcd_hint_knots / _hstem_knots in src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_glyf.spl). At 16 px Liberation Sans, FreeType's FT_LOAD_TARGET_LIGHT outline through libskia reproduces Chrome (Regular a..z 3 px, A..Z 2, digits 0; Bold a..z 2, A..Z 1) where the engine has 76, 57 and 83."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 1, "The outline must be exact to 1/64 px: o differs from FreeType by at most 1/64 px in y on seven points and still mismatches 8 px (Skia's quad chord count and quarter-row snaps flip). Measured sources: (a) an implied on-curve point must be the truncating midpoint of its two hinted 26.6 controls (FT_Outline_Decompose), not a font-unit midpoint hinted on its own (124 points in a..z, alone 77 -> 73 px); (b) points between edges need FreeType's integer arithmetic (af_glyph_hints_align_strong_points, weak points by IUP per contour); the engine maps every point through one global f64 knot map, so e's left extremum goes through the crossbar knots and lands 0.34 px low."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 2, "Needed: an integer port of FreeType af_latin vertical hinting (af_glyph_hints_reload flags and directions, segments, edges, blue edges, af_latin_hint_edges, align edge / strong / weak points, x by FT_MulFix, midpoints after hinting). OPEN QUESTION FIRST: the FreeType oracle does NOT hold at 13 and 14 px (Regular, 26 glyphs a line: 34 to 53 px against Chrome, e.g. A 9, T 4; the engine has 47 to 112). Either skrifa differs from FreeType at those sizes or the probe does; settle that before using FreeType as the oracle below 16 px."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 3, "Tools (lane scratch, not in git): /tmp/claude-1000/-home-yoon-dev-simple/f42fdf0c-b04a-464e-a276-b8701089e2fa/scratchpad/lcd1x/ : ftpath (FreeType hinted outline in 26.6), orc (outline -> libskia LCD mask -> best phase and offset per glyph against a black-on-white Chrome band; ORC_LUT = measured raw coverage -> Chrome level table), od.sh (engine outline vs FreeType point by point), lcddump.spl, pd / cc / blobs (text vs non-text, component sizes, per-glyph mismatch), fx2.html (spaced-glyph Chrome fixture). Build against ~/skia-n2/skia/out/simple-upstream-ganesh-vulkan (mk.sh). SkFont::getPath returns the UNHINTED outline; load through FreeType directly."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, P2, fixed, "web render: 1x LCD hinted outline is not FreeType/skrifa exact (largest 1x catalog cause); needs an af_latin integer port", src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_glyf.spl, 2262, test/01_unit/browser_engine/lcd_af_latin_hinted_outline_chrome159_spec.spl, 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 1x-lcd lane (work/webrender-1x-lcd-20261128): breakdown and design in doc/00_llm_process/feature_expert/web_render_css_parity/skill.md, section 2026-11-28 1x catalog breakdown by cause. Not started; too large for a page lane."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 af-latin lane (work/webrender-af-latin-hint-20261128): OPEN QUESTION settled. FreeType's light autohinter is Chrome at 13 and 14 px too. The 34 to 53 px were the probe: orc compared a window 3 px around each glyph blob, and at 13 px the LCD fringe of the next glyph falls inside it for narrow-bearing glyphs (A T V W Y k f j t). With a 1 px window (ORC_PAD=1) the FreeType outline through libskia gives 0 mismatching and 0 non-exact px on a..z, A..Z and 0..9 at 13, 14 and 16 px."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 2, "Fixed: src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_af_latin.spl is an integer port of af_latin in light mode (face metrics: standard width and six blue zones; scaled metrics; reload, segments, links, edges, blue edges, hint_edges, edge / strong / weak points). _glyph_outline feeds it the raw glyf points (SfntGlyfOutline.sgo_points) and decomposes the hinted points with truncating midpoints (_af_commands). The knot hinter (_lcd_hint_knots, _hstem_knots, _hint_commands) now serves only fonts behind the Devanagari gate (_lcd_area_font), whose outlines stay byte-identical to the base. Engine outline against FreeType 2.14, point for point at 0/64, 90 ASCII glyphs x 19 sizes (6..32 px) x 8 Liberation faces: equal on 101 of the 152 face-size cells; on the other 51 only i and j differ, by the lift of the dot that 2.14 has and Chrome does not (next line). Sans Regular and Serif Bold are also equal at 36, 40, 44 and 48 px."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 3, "Measured rules: the x-height threshold is 40/64 at every size (FreeType's increase-x-height is off by default; Chrome agrees: 8 px x is 4 rows); the non-base glyphs ^ _ ` ~ take no blue zone; FreeType 2.14's diacritic adjustment database is NOT in Chrome 159 (the dot of an 8 px i sits against the stem; accented letters match Chrome without it and mismatch with it), so it is left out. 1x catalog base 85ea9caddc5 -> head: overview 0.16 -> 0.02, html 0.29 -> 0.05, css-layout 0.40 -> 0.12, css-paint 0.35 -> 0.00, forms-media 0.34 -> 0.04, animation 0.34 -> 0.02, evidence 0.08 -> 0.00, tab-bar 0.02 -> 0.00; 4x unchanged. Rebased on 3cb5a3d3eeb (base -> head): 0.17 -> 0.03, 0.30 -> 0.06, 0.40 -> 0.12, 0.40 -> 0.06, 0.38 -> 0.08, 0.37 -> 0.05, 0.18 -> 0.10, 0.02 -> 0.00. Rebased on a3b55a1bc49 the head measures 0.02 0.02 0.09 0.00 0.04 0.00 0.00 0.00 (rows before 0.16 0.26 0.35 0.35 0.33 0.32 0.08 0.02)."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 4, "Left open as their own bugs: web_render_af_cedilla_hint_differs_from_chrome_2026-11-28, web_render_af_non_latin_styles_not_ported_2026-11-28 (superscript, Cyrillic, Greek, Devanagari), web_render_lcd_run_end_ink_column_not_painted_2026-11-28 (found on the way)."
    web_render_lcd_hinted_outline_not_freetype_exact_2026-11-28, 5, "close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/browser_engine/lcd_af_latin_hinted_outline_chrome159_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/browser_engine/lcd_af_latin_hinted_outline_chrome159_spec.spl"
